monom is a framework for building CLI tools. Its name is always lowercase.

Read `CLAUDE.md` before making changes — it is the working guide and links the
canonical documents (`constitution.md`, `architecture.md`, `terminology.md`).

This project is **not** spec-driven. Do not create specification documents,
change proposals, or task files. High-level decisions go in the canonical
documents; contested tradeoffs go in a `TRADEOFFS.md` beside the code.

Run `make check` to validate a change (build, vet, Go tests, shUnit2 e2e,
shellcheck). `make help` lists all targets.

Do not run `chmod +x` unless you got a "permission denied" error, then run it.
